  "worked_solution": "We know that \n\n$$\n\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying these formulae and the constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+3(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
